home security cameras they can be great  for monitoring deliveries  keeping an eye on your house and of  course spying on your cats in fact  around 14 of us households with  broadband now use an internet connected  camera and the us market for home  security cameras is projected to  continue growing rapidly through 2030  but their popularity has come at a cost  amazon's ring doorbell may not be as  private as you think hackers tapping  into those home cameras i'll leave you  and your family alone or i could do this  just this year amazon owned ring handed  over surveillance footage to law  enforcement 11 times without a warrant  or customer consent the company said the  request met its exception for  emergencies which it defines as danger  of death or serious physical injury and  since cats have nine lives and always  land on their feet i figured caneco a  manhattan-based cat cafe wouldn't be at  any risk of law enforcement stepping in  but there's a stereotype with cats and  it's that they're burglars and we'd like  to prove otherwise with this video  so that's why it's a perfect place to  come and outline some do's and don'ts  for you to consider when setting up and  installing some of the latest smart  surveillance cameras  of course joe golka caneco's cattery  guide was with us all day to ensure that  these rescued and adoptable cats were  happy and comfortable right you know you  can hang with me and that no real paws  were used  if you want your valuable recordings  shielded from prying eyes you should try  to enable end-to-end encryption  but what does that mean and what does it  do  to keep it simple let's say cameras  typically use one of two encryption  types there's standard encryption and  then there's end-to-end encryption  imagine two companies cat cam and dog  cam cat cam has end to end encryption  which means the only user with the key  to decrypt your video files is you well  you and anyone you share the account  with so end to end encryption protects  your data from hackers and prevents it  from being viewed by others such as law  enforcement or cat cam dog cam encrypts  your video when it's traveling from you  to company servers but it doesn't do it  end to end which means the company can  also hold the key to decrypt your  recordings if you're looking for  end-to-end encryption nicole recommends  a camera that works with apple's smart  home platform called homekit i like  these devices because end-to-end  encryption is on by default logitech's  circle view camera or doorbell are good  picks  they work indoor or outdoor and have  face recognition to identify different  people in your household or frequent  visitors  end-to-end encryption isn't limited to  just home kit cameras for instance you  can now enable it on some ring cameras  but it's not on by default and another  important note it's not available for  their battery-powered models and  disables some key features  no matter which brand you choose be sure  to use a secure password  don't point your camera at private  spaces security cameras usually have  ultra wide lenses that capture far more  than say a normal smartphone camera  would so it's important to consider the  expectation of privacy when installing  one ask yourself what would you be  comfortable with if you've got a  doorbell style security camera try not  to capture a shot into your neighbor's  front window and if there's a zone in  your camera's field of view you'd rather  not capture try enabling motion  detection or privacy zones cameras from  these brands all feature activity zone  triggering any home kit camera such as  those from eve or logitech ring google  nest and arlo ring devices can also set  up privacy zones which will black out  areas from being recorded in videos  do consider location factors if you're  looking to monitor an entire space  indoors it's best to keep your camera at  a higher location this will give you the  widest field of view then ask yourself  do i need night vision at my camera's  location if so make sure your security  camera has an infrared spotlight which  will enable it to capture video and  images in little to no light  also if your camera is being used as a  baby monitor or in a location where  silence is important it's worth noting  many security cameras can click when  activating their infrared light if  you're in a noise sensitive environment  try disabling night vision and buying a  separate infrared illuminator  and always be sure to let everyone in  your household or location know there's  a camera don't forget about hardware  quirks in the world of security cameras  you have outdoor cameras and indoor  cameras battery powered cameras can live  outside for months without having to be  recharged or having any pesky wires run  to them which makes it easy to forget  when they need to be charged  don't be a jerk or creep many brands let  you clip recordings which can then be  posted to social media  ring even has its own network called  neighbors  this for a place like caneco can be  great when they want to post clips of  their in-house influencers for public  consumption  but security cam users should always  think twice before posting to social  media that's because it's easy for  nefarious internet passers-by to  triangulate your location simply by  landmarks outside also a case of  mistaken identity or misunderstanding  can lead to an accidental tragedy  somebody getting fired all sorts of bad  things so before you post something  online take a breath think twice  and consider the outcome  [Music]
 

